# Docs metadata: README tables, SECURITY table and the "At a glance" box are generated from
# this (dev/gen-docs.py). One "key: value" per line.
emoji: ✂️
name: Screen snip
group: core
what: Select a rectangle of the window you're using, then copy it, save it, copy its text (OCR) or read it aloud (Narrate). Arrow Pad's Tools layer has a button for it.
why: SteamOS has no screenshot tool, and none of the usual ones can select a region inside VR.
changes: `frame-snip`, Tesseract (Homebrew), an app-menu entry; Piper comes from the Speech engine helper
access: Reads the picture of the window you're using (only when you start a snip)
survives-updates: Yes (everything is in your home folder and Homebrew)
undo: `./install.sh uninstall snip` (keeps Tesseract and your snips in `~/Pictures/Screenshots`)
